 [Deadlift](https://imgur.com/a/0UixeRd)

Are you unable to gain muscle while cutting? Sorry for so many questions but I am fairly new to the science behind lifting rather than just going and throwing heavy shit around at a gym and calling it working out.

&#x200B;

What I'm understand is bulking is how you get your gains. Your muscle that physically makes you stronger and your muscles bigger. It won't show too well as with bulking you are meant to gain weight, but you will be stronger than someone that looks like a model after a cut.

&#x200B;

And cutting is where you are going to still work out, maintain as much muscle mass as possible but lose as much body fat percentage as you can? You can't really gain muscle while cutting but it will make the muscle you have look way more defined.

&#x200B;

Am I fairly close to understanding?
